CONCEPT 1: CONTEXT WINDOWS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

DEFINITION
----------
The total number of tokens an LLM can "see" at once — everything in the
conversation: system prompt, user messages, tool calls, tool results, assistant
responses. The model has NO memory outside of it.

ANALOGY
-------
You're a consultant who can only read documents that fit on a single conference
table. When the table is full, adding a new document means removing an old one.
The moment a document leaves — you forget it completely. You don't know it's
missing. You confidently work with what's in front of you.

That's the LLM. It doesn't warn you when it's lost context. It just silently
makes worse decisions as the window fills.

CONTEXT WINDOW SIZES (mid-2026)
--------------------------------
Claude Sonnet 4.6   → 200,000 tokens  (largest mainstream)
GPT-4o              → 128,000 tokens
Gemini 1.5 Pro      → 1,000,000 tokens (quality degrades at extremes)
LLaMA 3 70B         → 128,000 tokens
Mistral Large       → 128,000 tokens

THE "LOST IN THE MIDDLE" PROBLEM
---------------------------------
LLMs attend strongly to the BEGINNING and END of context.
Information buried in the MIDDLE is frequently ignored.

Attention across a 100k token window:
████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░████████████
^-- START              MIDDLE                    END --^
(strong)               (weak)                  (strong)

→ Put critical instructions at the TOP of the system prompt, never in the middle.

THE KV CACHE — WHY IT MATTERS FOR COST
----------------------------------------
When the model processes a prompt, it computes a Key-Value (KV) cache for every
token. This is expensive. BUT: if the same tokens appear at the start of a new
request, the provider can REUSE the cached computation.

- Anthropic prompt caching saves ~90% on cached tokens
- OpenAI has similar caching
- Portkey's core cost optimization product is built on this

Cache-friendly prompt structure:
  [STABLE: system prompt]     ← cache this, never changes
  [DYNAMIC: user messages]    ← compute fresh each time

